          "text": "Hepatic panel",
          "is_correct": true
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "ANSWER: B Lithium is renally excreted and may cause renal concentrating defects due to buildup in the cells lining collecting ducts. Because hyponatremia may result in elevated lithium levels, electrolyte levels should be checked prior to treatment with lithium. Lithium may also cause hypothyroidism and leukocytosis and hence TSH and CBC should also be checked prior to treatment with lithium. A hepatic panel should be checked prior to initiation of treatment of medications metabolized in the liver, such as valproic acid.",
