      "explanation": "ANSWER: A Overvalued ideas are solitary, abnormal beliefs that are neither delusional nor obsessional, but with which the patient is preoccupied. Overvalued ideas are less strongly held than delusions, as in this example, in which the patient considers he might be wrong.",
